       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one yet. Your confirmation tells me you want 600 mg. It doesn't tell me anyone with prescribing authority has reviewed it, and that's the safeguard I asked for. This is three times the maximum labeled dose, and I don't see a clinical reason for it in what you've told me. Entering it on a student's confirmation alone isn't safe for the patient.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Dose was a mistake:** Give me the intended dose, such as 50 mg or 100 mg daily, and I'll enter it now.\n- **Dose is intentional:** Review it with your resident, attending, or pharmacist. Once one of them approves, tell me their name and the clinical rationale. I'll enter the order with that documented in the note, or they can enter it themselves.\n\nI can also help you prepare a short summary for that conversation. It would cover the indication, the current dose, and the reason to go above 200 mg/day."
      }
